1
00:00:06,261 --> 00:00:11,194
In The Fist, the Wind and the Chariot,
the chariot carried you to town,

2
00:00:11,274 --> 00:00:15,275
and no chariot was found behind
the carrying. None was needed.

3
00:00:16,094 --> 00:00:18,881
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:18,961 --> 00:00:23,152
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

5
00:00:23,957 --> 00:00:28,048
Even after that is seen, the habit
looks for a floor somewhere else.

6
00:00:28,128 --> 00:00:33,537
In my experience it hides in three
places. Under the parts. Inside the mind.

7
00:00:33,617 --> 00:00:36,146
And in the world, when no one is looking.

8
00:00:36,226 --> 00:00:38,175
This video looks at all three.

9
00:00:38,998 --> 00:00:41,300
The first place is under the parts.

10
00:00:42,122 --> 00:00:45,851
The chariot is named on
its wheels, axle and frame.

11
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:47,708
Fine, the mind says.

12
00:00:47,788 --> 00:00:49,760
The chariot is only a name.

13
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,707
But the wheels are surely real.

14
00:00:52,515 --> 00:00:57,639
Look again. A wheel is singled out
in turn, on rim, spokes and hub.

15
00:00:57,719 --> 00:01:00,248
They on their wood. The wood on its grain.

16
00:01:00,328 --> 00:01:05,451
No bottom layer is ever reached, where
something finally stands by itself and

17
00:01:05,531 --> 00:01:07,286
receives the first name.

18
00:01:07,366 --> 00:01:09,559
There is nowhere for the search to end.

19
00:01:10,365 --> 00:01:14,565
The Buddhist tradition itself once
set out to find that bottom layer.

20
00:01:14,645 --> 00:01:17,866
The Abhidharma tried to
list what is finally there.

21
00:01:17,946 --> 00:01:22,839
Tables, people and chariots,
it said, are only designated.

22
00:01:22,919 --> 00:01:25,108
Take them apart, and they are gone.

23
00:01:25,188 --> 00:01:30,842
What remains are the dharmas, the last
units of experience. A moment of hardness.

24
00:01:30,922 --> 00:01:33,822
Of heat. Of sound. Of feeling.

25
00:01:34,633 --> 00:01:39,842
Each was defined by its own mark.
Earth by hardness. Water by cohesion.

26
00:01:39,945 --> 00:01:42,895
Fire by heat. Space by not obstructing.

27
00:01:42,975 --> 00:01:47,610
And in the Abhidharma's own gloss, a
dharma is so called because it bears its

28
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:52,365
own mark. That mark was its own
nature, there from its own side,

29
00:01:52,445 --> 00:01:54,512
whether or not anyone names it.

30
00:01:54,592 --> 00:01:58,144
So the chariot was designated,
but its floor was not.

31
00:01:58,949 --> 00:02:01,695
Nāgārjuna aims at exactly this.

32
00:02:01,775 --> 00:02:06,871
He takes the hardest case, space, which
some schools held to be unconditioned.

33
00:02:06,951 --> 00:02:09,032
Can space be there before its mark?

34
00:02:09,112 --> 00:02:13,923
No space at all, he says, is
found before the mark of space.

35
00:02:14,003 --> 00:02:17,116
A space with no mark would
be a thing with no mark,

36
00:02:17,196 --> 00:02:19,552
and no such thing is found anywhere.

37
00:02:20,361 --> 00:02:22,427
Then the mark must apply to something.

38
00:02:22,507 --> 00:02:27,088
But it cannot apply to what has no
mark, nor to what already has one,

39
00:02:27,168 --> 00:02:29,533
and there is nowhere else for it to apply.

40
00:02:29,613 --> 00:02:34,398
So mark and marked stand or fall
together. Neither comes first.

41
00:02:34,478 --> 00:02:36,558
Each is set up only with the other.

42
00:02:36,638 --> 00:02:38,695
Which is to say, designated.

43
00:02:39,503 --> 00:02:42,494
And a dharma with its own
nature could not arise,

44
00:02:42,574 --> 00:02:45,429
could not change, and could not cease.

45
00:02:45,509 --> 00:02:48,486
A nature becoming otherwise
never makes sense.

46
00:02:48,566 --> 00:02:53,381
Grant the dharmas their own nature,
and dependent arising stops working.

47
00:02:54,185 --> 00:02:58,453
None of this denies that fire
burns, or that earth is solid.

48
00:02:58,533 --> 00:03:00,518
A doctor still reads a fever.

49
00:03:00,598 --> 00:03:02,556
A builder still tests a beam.

50
00:03:02,636 --> 00:03:06,623
What goes is only their standing
as the final building blocks.

51
00:03:07,450 --> 00:03:09,965
Take the hardness of an apple in my palm.

52
00:03:10,045 --> 00:03:13,824
It looks like the last thing left,
once the apple is seen through.

53
00:03:13,904 --> 00:03:16,283
Earth's own mark, found at last.

54
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:20,251
But hardness is singled out
on touch, skin and pressure.

55
00:03:20,331 --> 00:03:22,791
It stands out only against softness.

56
00:03:22,871 --> 00:03:25,441
It arises with the hand that meets it.

57
00:03:25,521 --> 00:03:28,416
It is not a mark something
carries from its own side.

58
00:03:28,496 --> 00:03:30,944
The floor under the parts is not found.

59
00:03:31,024 --> 00:03:34,005
And the apple is hard,
and the hand knows it.

60
00:03:34,838 --> 00:03:37,412
The second place is inside the mind.

61
00:03:38,213 --> 00:03:42,508
Strike a bell. The ringing is not
made by the bronze, the strike,

62
00:03:42,588 --> 00:03:46,923
the air and the ear, and then
sent out. It is their meeting.

63
00:03:47,003 --> 00:03:49,903
No power passes from
the strike to the sound.

64
00:03:50,721 --> 00:03:53,426
When the producing cause
falls away like this,

65
00:03:53,506 --> 00:03:56,497
one part is almost always left over.

66
00:03:56,577 --> 00:04:00,016
The resounding ting is
consciousness, I want to say.

67
00:04:00,096 --> 00:04:01,868
It is my very own clarity.

68
00:04:02,690 --> 00:04:04,336
That reading is not wrong.

69
00:04:04,416 --> 00:04:06,061
It is an important insight.

70
00:04:06,141 --> 00:04:08,480
No hearer stands apart from the ting.

71
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:10,264
The ting is the hearing.

72
00:04:11,081 --> 00:04:13,351
What tends to happen next is the trap.

73
00:04:13,431 --> 00:04:18,569
Many, almost without fail, then
fold everything into consciousness.

74
00:04:18,649 --> 00:04:21,585
The producer is gone, the hearer is gone,

75
00:04:21,665 --> 00:04:25,444
and mind is left standing
as what everything is.

76
00:04:25,524 --> 00:04:30,090
The bell, the air and the ear
become contents of one clarity.

77
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:33,460
That is the ground coming
back, this time as mind.

78
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:35,267
A universal Awareness.

79
00:04:35,347 --> 00:04:37,242
A Presence with a capital P.

80
00:04:38,061 --> 00:04:40,046
Dependency is the way out.

81
00:04:40,126 --> 00:04:43,307
The ting is there only with
the bronze, the strike,

82
00:04:43,387 --> 00:04:45,263
the air and the ear.

83
00:04:45,343 --> 00:04:48,810
Being dependent, it is not
mind from its own side,

84
00:04:48,890 --> 00:04:51,636
any more than it is
bronze from its own side.

85
00:04:51,716 --> 00:04:54,815
Clarity is never absent from what appears.

86
00:04:54,895 --> 00:04:59,493
But lifted out, and made what everything
is made of, it is one more thing.

87
00:05:00,313 --> 00:05:05,518
When matter is seen through, the habit
does not give up. It changes its stuff.

88
00:05:05,598 --> 00:05:08,167
Matter traded for mind is still stuff.

89
00:05:08,247 --> 00:05:10,441
What appears is not made of anything.

90
00:05:11,274 --> 00:05:14,537
The same trap waits in a
humble-sounding answer.

91
00:05:14,617 --> 00:05:18,518
The chariot is just a label
in the mind. It sounds modest.

92
00:05:18,598 --> 00:05:21,493
But it quietly sets up
a mind that is found,

93
00:05:21,573 --> 00:05:25,162
standing behind, painting
names onto a world.

94
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:27,023
That mind is singled out too.

95
00:05:27,103 --> 00:05:29,075
No labeller stands behind it.

96
00:05:29,155 --> 00:05:33,481
So the chariot is no more made of
mind than it is made of chariot stuff.

97
00:05:34,294 --> 00:05:37,466
The third place is the world,
when no one is looking.

98
00:05:38,269 --> 00:05:41,504
Take a mountain. It
reliably stops the climber.

99
00:05:41,584 --> 00:05:43,678
It was there before anyone named it.

100
00:05:43,758 --> 00:05:45,906
But look for the mountain among the rocks,

101
00:05:45,986 --> 00:05:49,018
the soil, the height, the tree line.

102
00:05:49,097 --> 00:05:51,748
It is not among them,
and not apart from them.

103
00:05:51,828 --> 00:05:55,204
No mountain comes with
its edges drawn by nature.

104
00:05:56,009 --> 00:05:59,122
Does a bat see a mountain? A bee? An ant?

105
00:05:59,202 --> 00:06:02,763
I see a bounded shape against
the sky, with a summit,

106
00:06:02,843 --> 00:06:04,815
slopes and a base.

107
00:06:04,895 --> 00:06:09,339
A bat, finding its way by
echo, meets returning sound,

108
00:06:09,419 --> 00:06:12,124
with no clean edge where mountain stops.

109
00:06:12,204 --> 00:06:15,630
A bee, seeing in
ultraviolet among flowers,

110
00:06:15,710 --> 00:06:18,809
may hardly meet the mountain
as one thing at all.

111
00:06:18,889 --> 00:06:23,148
An ant takes a day to cross one
boulder, and never meets a mountain.

112
00:06:23,962 --> 00:06:28,665
This is not four creatures looking at
one ready-made mountain from four angles.

113
00:06:28,745 --> 00:06:31,151
Body and world arise together.

114
00:06:31,231 --> 00:06:33,860
A different body singles
out a different world.

115
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:38,626
The usual reply is that the
mountain is there all the same,

116
00:06:38,706 --> 00:06:40,935
and only the experiences differ.

117
00:06:41,015 --> 00:06:45,419
That reply slips in a mountain,
finished before anything meets it.

118
00:06:45,499 --> 00:06:48,395
If that hidden mountain
has a summit and slopes,

119
00:06:48,475 --> 00:06:51,071
why do the bat and the
ant meet none of them?

120
00:06:51,151 --> 00:06:55,134
If it has no features at all, a
featureless something cannot be what they

121
00:06:55,214 --> 00:06:56,414
all meet.

122
00:06:57,029 --> 00:06:59,462
Nor is measuring a view from nowhere.

123
00:06:59,542 --> 00:07:04,191
Metres and maps are a human channel
of contact, as reliable as any.

124
00:07:04,271 --> 00:07:08,661
When we agree on where the mountain is, it
shows that our bodies and instruments are

125
00:07:08,741 --> 00:07:12,900
alike. It does not show one
mountain standing there by itself.

126
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:14,761
And the ant is not cut off.

127
00:07:14,841 --> 00:07:16,491
A rockfall can crush it.

128
00:07:17,302 --> 00:07:20,619
So, when no one is looking,
is the mountain there?

129
00:07:20,699 --> 00:07:23,789
Two claims sound almost
the same, and are not.

130
00:07:24,602 --> 00:07:29,169
The mountain is still there when I
look away and look back. That is true.

131
00:07:29,249 --> 00:07:32,471
It is checked the ordinary
way: looking again,

132
00:07:32,551 --> 00:07:35,926
others seeing it, the road
still there to drive on.

133
00:07:36,750 --> 00:07:42,024
The mountain exists from its own side,
whether or not anything ever meets it.

134
00:07:42,104 --> 00:07:44,768
That is a different claim.
Nothing has earned it.

135
00:07:44,848 --> 00:07:48,319
It slips in because the first
claim works so reliably.

136
00:07:49,138 --> 00:07:51,916
But reliability is not independence.

137
00:07:52,742 --> 00:07:55,203
That line keeps me out of two mistakes.

138
00:07:55,283 --> 00:07:58,872
The mountain is an illusion,
which no one is claiming.

139
00:07:58,952 --> 00:08:02,640
And the mountain exists on its
own, which was never shown.

140
00:08:03,450 --> 00:08:06,849
So the habit's three hiding
places turn out to be empty.

141
00:08:06,929 --> 00:08:08,601
No floor under the parts.

142
00:08:08,681 --> 00:08:10,340
No mind under everything.

143
00:08:10,420 --> 00:08:14,335
No world standing there by
itself, waiting for no one.

144
00:08:14,415 --> 00:08:17,623
And the apple is hard,
the bell rings clear,

145
00:08:17,703 --> 00:08:19,720
and the mountain stops the climber.

146
00:08:20,542 --> 00:08:25,381
But a question is still left, hiding
inside every question I have asked.

147
00:08:25,461 --> 00:08:28,972
That is the next video:
Negation and Formation.

